  "note": "Sky1 arm64 DEFAULT kernel under the unified 7.3 policy: r291 = the v7.3.0 FINAL pin. The r290 series (27 numbered patches 0001-0011 + 0013-0028, plus the consolidated port patch) was replayed onto the upstream v7.3 tag (c03c1a14) and applies cleanly: 28/28 patches, 0 conflicts, 0 rejects, 0 fuzz. The same replay on v7.3-rc7 differs only in the 212 files upstream changed between the two tags, so every Sky1 change is carried across intact. Two code-review findings were actioned in the port patch: an unbounded strcpy in get_cpuname_by_dmi (arch/arm64/kernel/cix_dmi.c) is now strscpy bounded by the allocation size; the reported kzalloc_obj(*r) issue in drivers/acpi/scan.c is NOT a defect (kzalloc_obj is an upstream API taking the pointee TYPE via typeof, and *r there is the type, not a dereference -- upstream uses the same idiom in the same file). BUILD NOT RUN: no Yocto environment on the staging host, so Module.symvers / verify-overlay-modversions have NOT been executed and the debs, image, build_id, modules and overlay entries below are null. 7.3.0-sky1-ncz is a NEW KVER, so the r290 overlay *.ko files cannot be reused -- all six must be rebuilt and re-verified before this manifest is valid. Do not publish.",
